      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/nematobrycon_palmeri_wild_en/",
      "html": "<p>The emperor tetra (Nematobrycon palmeri) has for decades been one of the most beloved tetra species of all, thanks to its great beauty and interesting behaviour.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/nematobrycon_palmeri_wild_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species is available all year round as captive-bred fish. Wild-collected fish, on the other hand, are available only seasonally. Wild-collected and captive-bred emperor tetras differ, as in most tetra species, mainly in body shape: wild fish are much more slender than captive-bred ones, because food in the wild is far less abundant than it usually is in aquaria. In coloration there is no difference between wild and captive-bred fish: both are very beautiful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/nematobrycon_palmeri_wild_en/",
      "html": "<p>Wild fish are imported from Colombia.</p>"
    }
  ],
